<title>USA: U.S. Rep Roberts wants EEP resumption.</title>
<headline>U.S. Rep Roberts wants EEP resumption.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. House Agriculture Committee Chairman Pat Roberts said Wednesday the U.S. administration should consider resuming export subsidies under the Export Enhancement Program because of higher world supplies.</p>
<p>Roberts, R-Kan, told reporters the administration should have some contingency plans in case of price drops and said the administration should send an early signal to the European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;We could get to the situation very quickly where you could get some very precipitous price declines,&quot; Roberts said.</p>
</text>
